{"id": "swebq0023", "pool": "swebq", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Leonardo da Vinci was a master of many different art forms. He created incredible paintings like The Last Supper and the Mona Lisa, which are still famous today. He also did lots of drawings, including detailed sketches of human anatomy, animals, and machines. So he was not only an artist but also an in ventor and scientist.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 15, "carrier_ended": null}
